<title>USA: Sewage, trash seen as source for fertilizer, water.</title>
<headline>Sewage, trash seen as source for fertilizer, water.</headline>
<byline>Charles Abbott</byline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trash and sewage -- two munincipal headaches around the world -- could form a valuable water and fertilizer source for farmers, researchers said Monday at a World Bank conference.</p>
<p>The result, they said, would be larger food output and fewer worries about overflowing landfills. It also could mean less disease if farmers had &quot;cleaner&quot; water supplies instead of the polluted water now used for irrigation in parts of the world.</p>
</text>
